You know what's so funny? Mouse, louse, house, fox, ox: all are
perfectly Germanic words. Umlaut is a typically Germanic phenomenon;
plurals in both -en and -es are Germanic. -en sounds odd to you because
English dropped most of them, but Dutch and German have kept it; Dutch
also has -s, and German -er (and so, IIRC, have the Nordic languages, as
their normal plural form). Only "box" is ultimately from Greek, and it's
perfectly regular in English...

